// The alternatives of an arm are separated by or. A comma between literal
// patterns is a parse error (spec/02-syntax.md, Extended match arm
// patterns, "Alternatives").
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The try makes a
// run-time fault print, so an implementation that runs the program fails
// this probe.
try {
    print match 2 { case 1, 2 => "small" case _ => "other" };
} catch (e) {
    print e.kind;
}

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
